Reason: flash-03 mkfs log proves USERDATA remained mounted through stacked /sdcard aliases; optional data format swallowed the error and installer returned RC=0. Require a real format and fail safely when aliases cannot be unmounted.
Affected: platform/exynos9810/installer/repartition/format_partitions.sh; scripts/internal/verify_exynos9810_flashable.sh.
Verify: shell syntax; simulated stacked/canonical aliases, busy mount and mkfs failure propagation; verifier rejects old optional script. Live flash-03 uses unchanged patch0017 ZIP plus explicit TWRP Format Data after all aliases are unmounted, verified by new UUID and missing old settings/probes. This patch is for subsequent packaging and is not retroactively included in flash-03 ZIP.
Rollback: reverse patch; never treat installer success or ext4 TYPE alone as proof of fresh data. No kernel/blob changes.

